# Chaos wall/building cinematic workflow

## Scope

This workflow turns preserved Static Mesh inputs into native Geometry
Collections, records real solver-driven destruction to native Chaos Cache
Collections, and drives those caches from native Level Sequences and Movie
Render Queue. UnrealMCP is an authoring tool only. Final assets must load,
play, cook, package, and render without the UnrealMCP plugin.

All generated samples use:

- asset root `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ChaosDestructionLearning/Cinematic`
- Unreal Engine 5.6.1
- 30 fps display rate, 24000 tick resolution, and 30 Hz fixed physics
- Root Mesh Proxy through `UGeometryCollectionRootProxyRenderer`
- `EnableNanite=false`; Nanite is out of scope

## Required samples

| ID | Sample | Minimum gate |
|---|---|---|
| S01 | Single wall | 64 rigid leaves, collision and trace destruction, Root Proxy transition, 2-second cache and Sequence |
| S02 | Door/window wall | 96 leaves; opening ray misses 20/20 and jamb/wall ray hits 20/20 before and after fracture |
| S03 | Anchored small building | 128 leaves; 10-30% foundation pieces anchored within 0.5 cm and 0.5 degrees while upper pieces move at least 10 cm or break |
| S04 | Sequential multi-storey building | 256 leaves, hierarchy depth at least 3, three collapse stages separated by at least 10 frames |
| S05 | Reused-cache shots | one exact cache object path reused by at least three sections/camera cuts with different offsets or play rates |

## Evidence contract

Every command keeps `operation_status`, `assertion_status`, and
`learning_verdict` separate. A successful dispatch is not proof that a later
physics or Sequencer result occurred. Missing live evidence is `BLOCKED`; an
executed but incorrect result is `FAIL`.

State hashes are SHA-256 over sorted `(component path, transform index,
position, rotation, scale)` records. Position is quantized to 0.1 cm and
rotation to 0.1 degrees. CRC32 or hashes computed from expected rather than
observed transforms are not accepted.

Each sample manifest records asset paths, manager/field actor identities,
cache names, binding GUIDs, dirty-package snapshots, source package SHA-256
before and after, Asset Registry dependencies, editor/build logs, and raw
performance samples.

## Acceptance gates

1. Source and output paths differ. Source hashes are unchanged, source
   packages remain clean, transforms are finite with nonzero scale, and the
   assembled bounds match input instance bounds within 1%.
2. Fracture has one root, no invalid parent/cycle/triangle/non-manifold defect,
   the required sample leaf/depth count, and the same hierarchy digest when
   repeated with the same seed.
3. The Anchor Field is serialized into the GC component initialization fields
   before fresh PIE. Its foundation and upper-structure motion satisfy the S03
   gate.
4. Trace strain produces 20/20 intentional hits with a valid component and
   `FHitResult.Item`; 20/20 intentional misses do not change break count. A
   later physics tick has velocity-direction dot product greater than 0.5 and
   increased broken or released state.
5. Tiny threshold 0.04 removes or explains all candidates, reduces collision
   shapes by at least 20%, preserves bounds/volume within 1%, and does not close
   the S02 opening.
6. Sleep and Break removal are tested separately within one fixed tick. Eight
   simultaneous breaks with `PerAdvanceBreaksAllowed=2` process at most two per
   frame and eventually process all eight. Baseline/controlled release limits
   and full setting restoration pass in all five runs.
7. Root Proxy arrays and renderer are valid, Nanite is off, proxy-only changes
   to native GC within one frame of real fracture with no double-render frame.
   A 32-instance A/B reduces draw calls by at least 20%, with RenderThread/GPU
   median regression no worse than 5%.
8. Every manager observes one native `UChaosCacheCollection` entry with a
   unique cache name, and source cache assets are clean after recording.
9. Every cache contains at least 60 frames and at least 2.0 seconds, and its
   observed transform tracks vary over time.
10. Every native `ULevelSequence` reads back 30 fps/24000, a valid playback
    range, and a camera cut after asset reload.
11. A manager possessable resolves to the exact `AChaosCacheManager`; a native
    Chaos Cache track/section refers to the same manager cache and remains
    resolved after reload.
12. Before section start the state is the rest hash; at the chosen start frame
    it equals the expected cache-time hash. Offset, play rate, reverse, and
    inclusive/exclusive ranges read back within one tick.
13. Frames `[0, 15, 30, 45, 60]` evaluated forward, reverse, and random order at
    least twice yield the same SHA-256 per frame regardless of visit history.
14. S05 runs a real MRQ job at 640x360 for 60 frames. Decode failures, zero-byte
    frames, and black frames are zero; repeated key-frame perceptual hashes
    differ by at most 4 while Chaos state hashes are identical.
15. Package, cache, manager, and binding identifiers do not collide. S05 uses
    one cache object, not cloned caches made to appear equivalent.

## Performance acceptance

All A/B cases run five times with the same map, camera, warmup, actor count,
fixed physics, and rendering settings. Evidence retains all raw values plus
median and p95; fixed delta does not replace wall-clock frame timing.

For S04 controlled playback/runtime:

- peak active bodies are at most 256 and at most 75% of baseline
- `STAT_AdvanceClustering` median is at most baseline times 1.05
- `STAT_AdvanceClustering` p95 is at most baseline
- GameThread p95 is at most 33.33 ms
- at most 5% of frames exceed 33.33 ms
- no more than two over-budget frames are consecutive

The budget is fixed before measurement and is not relaxed after seeing a
result.

## Disallowed proof shortcuts

Do not force a Root Proxy broken state, write transforms every frame, force
kinematic state merely to claim cache playback suppression, call manager
`SetStartTime` during Sequencer validation, generate expected transforms or
hashes instead of sampling cache output, substitute viewport screenshots for
MRQ, hide wall-clock drops with fixed delta, or clone cache objects for S05.
One declared initial impulse/velocity and real External Strain are allowed;
subsequent state must come from Chaos, the Cache Manager, or Sequencer.

## NoMCP promotion gate

The clean host must not contain `Plugins/UnrealMCP`. `ChaosCaching` and
`MovieRenderPipeline` remain explicitly enabled in the project independently.
All five maps and Sequences must reload, resolve bindings, play, render through
MRQ, cook/package, and exit cleanly with zero missing-class/link errors, zero
dirty packages, and zero Asset Registry dependency hits for `/Script/UnrealMCP`,
`/UnrealMCP`, or other MCP-only names.

## Current status

The acceptance contract is frozen. Until the isolated live suite, MRQ output,
five-run measurements, and NoMCP host checks all pass, the cinematic workflow
remains `BLOCKED` rather than being promoted from configuration-only evidence.
